From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:14:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 140/142] rtl: win64: release an exception the default handler
 unwinds for when a finally block replaces it

The outermost handler pushes an unhandled exception on the exception
object stack and unwinds to the outermost frame, but left the entry's
UnwindFrame nil, so ReleaseAbandonedExceptions never released it: when a
finally block on the way raised an exception that a handler caught, the
replaced exception and its entry stayed on the stack (RaiseList) and the
object was never freed. Mark the entry as unwinding from the handler, as
__FPC_specific_handler does.
---
 rtl/win64/seh64.inc | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rtl/win64/seh64.inc b/rtl/win64/seh64.inc
index 1b9e7ac3..86ae02b4 100644
--- a/rtl/win64/seh64.inc
+++ b/rtl/win64/seh64.inc
@@ -545,6 +545,9 @@ begin
     end;
 {$endif CPUX86_64}
     PushException(rec,context,obj,True,frame);
+    { the unwind runs from here: a finally block that raises an exception caught
+      before the outermost frame abandons it, and the entry with it }
+    ExceptObjectStack^.UnwindFrame:=@obj;
     RtlUnwindEx(frame, @L1, @rec, nil, dispatch.ContextRecord, dispatch.HistoryTable);
   end
   else if (rec.ExceptionFlags and EXCEPTION_TARGET_UNWIND)<>0 then
